Mission Control keeps what a Claude Code session's turn did (from its hooks):
the files it wrote or edited (Write/Edit/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit, at most 5)
and whether its last tool call failed; a turn that fails (StopFailure) while
another session is on screen is unseen too. The Workbench gets them per
terminal (sessions[id].turn: files, failed, error). The page sorts its
sessions out (it also reads their last answers for a PR link) and sends its
top kind with the chats report; the sidebar's Workbench row shows that kind's
icon and count (amber permission/question, red error, blue PR/result/done),
or Mission Control's own counts for an older page.

